<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-020>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-020" ;
  triage:title "Every task-path error is flattened to a bare anyhow string, collapsing the CLI exit-code contract to 1 (aka RBP-F102)" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. Every task-path error is flattened to a bare anyhow string, collapsing the CLI exit-code contract to 1. Doc says: The CLI maintains a stable exit-code contract (exit_code_for_error, crates/atm/src/main.rs:82-85), and BA.4's stage table distinguishes rejection modes by behaviour. Code does: task.rs:267, task.rs:350 and send.rs:256-262 re-wrap the AtmError as `anyhow::anyhow!(error.to_string())`, destroying the downcast, so exit_code_for_error falls through to its map_or(1, ...) default for every failure on the whole `atm task` surface. Recommendation: Propagate AtmError (or attach it as an anyhow source) through the task path so exit codes and tests can discriminate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "best-practices" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm/src/commands/task.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2A821M48VWSZ0JGXMA4WWZ7, 2026-09-12T07:24:38Z): fixed by cipher at 33894ac10 (bundled with CPR-019). quality-mgr consolidated QA (BA-REVIEW-QA-1789194730, PR #1425 comment 5645308114, 2026-09-12T10:24:25Z): partial fix -- direct `atm task` subcommands (task.rs) now preserve AtmError for exit-code discrimination, but crates/atm/src/commands/send.rs:256-262 still flattens it to a bare anyhow!(error.to_string()) on the `atm send --task-id`/`--task-complete` alias path. Team-lead independently confirmed via git show 9774e113c:crates/atm/src/commands/send.rs (task_alias branch at the map_err on build_request_with_mode). Reopened as post-landing backlog (Important, partial); the task.rs-surface closure stands." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "RBP-F102" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-020/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-020/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-020/3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

